\b Document Extraction Test Fixture\b0\par
\par
\b Purpose\b0\par
This file is synthetic. It exists so the document-extraction tests have a real container in each supported format to parse. Nothing here describes a real person, organisation, product or event.\par
\par
\b Structure\b0\par
The extractors are checked on three things: that text comes out at all, that the reported metadata matches the format, and that word counts are positive. This document therefore carries several paragraphs of ordinary prose rather than a single line, so that truncation behaviour can be exercised as well.\par
\par
\b Unicode\b0\par
A few non-ASCII characters are included on purpose: cafe\u769?, na\u239?ve, \u252?ber, \u8212? an em dash \u8212? and a curly quote \u8220?like this\u8221?.\par
